menu "Voice Inventory Query Configuration"

    # NOTE: there is deliberately no auth-style option. The IMS API documents
    # `Authorization: Bearer <key>` as the only scheme, so inventory_api.c always sends
    # that. A configurable choice here would just be a way to get it wrong.

    config INV_SNTP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "SNTP sync timeout (ms)"
        default 15000
        help
            HTTPS certificate validation compares the cert's validity window against
            the system clock. This board boots at the epoch (no RTC battery fitted),
            so without SNTP every TLS handshake fails as "certificate not yet valid".
            Plain http:// works regardless.


    config VOICE_LED_GPIO
        int "Indicator LED GPIO"
        default 26
        help
            Lights when an inventory fetch SUCCEEDS, stays dark when it fails.

            This board has NO GPIO-controllable onboard LED -- its only discrete LED is
            the hardwired PWR indicator, and every other LED-named net belongs to the
            IP101 Ethernet PHY or the CH334F USB hub. So an external LED plus a
            220-470 ohm series resistor is required: GPIO26 is header pin 31, with GND
            on pin 30 or 34. Do not use pin 35 (GPIO53 = audio power-amp enable).

    config VOICE_LED_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "LED is active-low"
        default n

    config INV_SEARCH_TERM
        string "Search term for the demo query"
        default "arduino"
        help
            The term sent as /api/v1/products?search=<term>. In Phase 4 this comes from
            the recognised voice command instead; a plain word like "arduino" is far
            easier for MultiNet than an alphanumeric product code.

    config INV_POLL_SECONDS
        int "Seconds between demo queries"
        default 20
        range 5 600
        help
            IMS allows 120 requests/minute per key and its docs say to poll from ONE
            server rather than per browser. The board is that server; browsers receive
            pushes over the dashboard WebSocket. 20 s is far inside the limit.


    config INV_SOFTAP_ENABLE
        bool "Also broadcast a SoftAP for the dashboard"
        default y
        help
            Runs the C6 in WIFI_MODE_APSTA: still joined to your Wi-Fi for the IMS API,
            while ALSO broadcasting its own network you can attach to directly.

            This exists because the office SSID has AP client isolation -- unicast
            station-to-station traffic is dropped, so nothing on that network can reach
            a server on this board (proven: broadcast arrives, unicast does not). The
            SoftAP sidesteps it without needing any router change.

            A device attached to the SoftAP has no internet route; it only needs the
            dashboard. The board keeps its own uplink for the API.

    config INV_SOFTAP_SSID
        string "SoftAP SSID"
        default "ESP32-P4-Inventory"
        depends on INV_SOFTAP_ENABLE

    config INV_SOFTAP_PASSWORD
        string "SoftAP password (8-63 chars, or empty for an open network)"
        default "inventory123"
        depends on INV_SOFTAP_ENABLE
        help
            Not a real secret -- it only gates access to a read-only dashboard on a
            local radio, and it is committed in sdkconfig.defaults. The IMS API key is
            NOT reachable from the dashboard, so an attacker on this AP cannot obtain it.

    config INV_VOICE_SVC_URL
        string "Voice service base URL (Whisper STT + Piper TTS)"
        default "http://10.10.8.51:8099"
        help
            Runs on the infra VM. POST /stt takes raw PCM (16-bit signed LE, 16 kHz,
            mono, no WAV header, max 15 s) and returns {"text": ...}; POST /tts takes
            {"text": ...} and returns PCM in the same format.

            The service allowlists this board's IP, so a 403 FORBIDDEN_NETWORK means
            the board's DHCP address changed and the server needs updating. A timeout
            instead means the cross-subnet route is down.

    config INV_MIC_GAIN_DB
        int "Microphone input gain (dB)"
        default 42
        range 0 48
        help
            Analog gain on the onboard SMD microphone. Project 22 used 24 dB and found
            speech had to be loud and close: -27 dBFS was recognised, -41 dBFS never
            was. 32 dB is a measured step up from that to widen the usable margin.

            MEASURED 2026-10-05 with real speech at 32 dB: the ONE transcript that came
            back correct was captured at -26.5 dBFS; everything from -36 dBFS down
            produced Whisper hallucinations ("They grow." repeated 23 times) or
            "no speech heard". Project 22 independently measured the same -27 dBFS
            threshold with a completely different recogniser, so this is a capture-level
            limit, not a model limit. Raised to 42 dB to close that ~10 dB gap.

            The idle noise floor is about -48 dBFS, so going much higher amplifies room
            noise as much as speech.

    config INV_RECORD_SECONDS
        int "Seconds to record per question"
        default 4
        range 1 15
        help
            A spoken question is typically 2-4 s. The service rejects anything over
            15 s with HTTP 413, which it may deliver as a connection reset mid-upload.

    config INV_MIN_SPEECH_DBFS
        int "Minimum level to bother transcribing (negative dBFS)"
        default -40
        range -70 -10
        help
            Recordings quieter than this are discarded WITHOUT calling the service.

            This is not an optimisation, it is a correctness guard. Fed near-silence,
            Whisper does not return nothing -- it hallucinates repetitive text
            ("Thank you very much" twelve times). Measured here: every capture below
            -35 dBFS produced either a hallucination or an empty result, and not one
            produced usable text. Sending that audio can only mislead.

    config INV_CACHE_MAX_AGE_S
        int "Refresh the catalogue cache after this many seconds"
        default 120
        range 15 3600
        help
            The catalogue is fetched once and matched locally, so a question costs no
            API call. This bounds how stale an answer can be. IMS allows 120 requests
            per minute; at 120 s between refreshes we use 0.5 per minute.

    config INV_WAV_SINK_URL
        string "Mirror each capture to this URL (empty = off)"
        default "http://192.168.68.104:8077/"
        help
            Diagnostic. POSTs every recorded WAV to a listener so the audio can be
            heard and measured off-board.

            This exists because transcription failures are untreatable from the serial
            log alone: clipping, a wrong channel, a sample-rate mismatch and a DC
            offset all look identical from here. Set empty to disable.

    config INV_MIC_CHANNELS
        int "Channels to open the microphone with (1 = mono, 2 = stereo+deinterleave)"
        default 1
        range 1 2
        help
            Project 22 opened the ES8311 in STEREO and fed both channels to AFE, letting
            AFE pick the microphone. It never validated extracting mono itself.

            If the codec actually delivers MONO frames while we ask for 2 channels and
            take every other sample, the result is a half-rate, aliased signal -- which
            measures as noise (zero-crossing rate 5000-7500/s where speech is 500-3000)
            and makes Whisper hallucinate. Set 1 to read mono directly.

endmenu
